# 0002. One branch per lab on top of a shared skeleton

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-19

Each lab is a branch (`lab1` … `lab6`) grown from the same empty ASP.NET Core project, so every
lab can be checked out and run on its own; `main` keeps only that skeleton.

## Technical details
- **`main`**: `dotnet new` MVC skeleton (`Web.sln`, `Web/Program.cs`, `Startup.cs`,
  `appsettings*.json`, netcoreapp3.1) and the README.
- **Lab branches**: `lab1` calculator service; `lab2` forms; `lab3` validation; `lab4`
  authentication and password reset; `lab5` hospital database with EF Core and SQL Server;
  `lab6` forum and blog with ASP.NET Identity, file and folder management. Each later lab
  builds on the previous one's history.
- **Build output**: the 2020 commits tracked `Web/bin` and `Web/obj`; `main` now ignores them,
  the lab branches keep their old copies (they are the submitted state).
- **Databases**: labs 5-6 use `Server=(localdb)\mssqllocaldb` (Windows LocalDB) with trusted
  connections; no passwords are stored.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: .NET Core 3.1, ASP.NET Core MVC, EF Core with SQL Server, ASP.NET Identity.
- Alternatives: one folder per lab on `main` (all labs buildable at once, but duplicated
  projects); merging labs into `main` (would hide the per-lab state that was graded).
